# /etc/rancher/k3s/config.yaml.d/30-image-gc.yaml
# Managed by Ansible (k3s_node_config.yml). Manual edits will be overwritten.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# containerd never garbage-collects images on its own, and kubelet's image GC
# only fires once the image filesystem crosses imageGCHighThresholdPercent —
# which defaults to 85. The nodes sat at 81-83% for months: parked just under
# the trigger, accumulating every image Renovate ever bumped and every digest a
# rolling tag ever orphaned. By 2026-08-12 worker-1 held **375 images / 301 GB**
# with only 74 referenced by any container.
#
# That was not merely wasted disk. worker-1's VM disk is a 400 G raw file on
# pve-mammoth's local SPCC, so a full guest disk stopped the nightly vzdump from
# skipping zero blocks — the backup went from 44 s to 28 minutes of sustained
# reads, saturated the drive, starved mon.pve-mammoth, and surfaced as
# BLUESTORE_SLOW_OP_ALERT on osd.0. See the incident record on the wiki:
# operations/common-incidents/2026-08-12-containerd-bloat-backup-ceph-slowops
#
# Lowering the ceiling to 70 makes kubelet reclaim on its own long before the
# guest disk fills, so the cleanup stops depending on someone noticing.
#
# ⚠️ low MUST be < high. The defaults are high=85 / low=80, so setting only
# `image-gc-high-threshold=70` leaves low=80 > high=70 and **kubelet refuses to
# start**. Always set both.
#
# Reclaim band: GC triggers at 70% and frees until the image filesystem is back
# under 60%. kubelet only removes images that are NOT in use by any container,
# oldest-unused first, and respects imageMinimumGCAge (default 2m).
#
# ⚠️ Note for the masters: they run on 48 G disks and were at 72-74% with
# 20-26 GB of containerd images when this landed, so GC fires there immediately
# on first apply. That is the intended effect — but it is not a no-op, and a
# cached image whose upstream has withdrawn public access will not come back.
# Two such images were found on 2026-08-12 (a Patreon-gated ghcr package and
# Zenika's retired GCR mirror); both are resolved, but audit before assuming a
# reclaim is free.
kubelet-arg:
  - "image-gc-high-threshold=70"
  - "image-gc-low-threshold=60"
